  "description": "The 2026 Ohio gubernatorial election will be held on November 3, 2026, to elect the next governor of Ohio. Incumbent Republican Governor Mike DeWine is term-limited and ineligible to seek a third consecutive term. The open-seat race features Republican nominee Vivek Ramaswamy, a biotech entrepreneur and former 2024 presidential candidate, and Democratic nominee Dr. Amy Acton, the former Ohio Department of Health director who led the state's COVID-19 response, along with Libertarian nominee Don Kissick. This is one of the most closely watched gubernatorial races in the country, as Ohio has not elected a Democratic governor since 2006, and the race is expected to be the most expensive in state history with national implications for both parties.",
